<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  net.kingfisher.fleet — bring the fleet up at login and keep it up.

  WHY launchd AND NOT A WATCHDOG SCRIPT. macOS already ships the supervisor, so
  writing one would be a second implementation of a solved problem. More to the
  point: any watchdog this repo launched would itself be a child of whatever
  launched it, which is the exact defect H6 records — three lanes dead with
  .heartbeat.* 35 minutes stale because the supervisor inherited the lifetime of
  the session that started it. launchd is the one process that does not.

  WHY StartInterval AND NOT KeepAlive. bringup.sh EXITS once the fleet is up;
  KeepAlive would treat that success as a crash and respawn it in a tight loop.
  StartInterval re-runs it every 5 minutes instead, and because bringup.sh is
  idempotent — it refuses to relaunch a callsign that is already held (H8) — a
  re-run is a no-op when everything is healthy and a repair when a lane has died.
  That is the H6 alarm and the H6 heal in one mechanism, with no new code.

  WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. It does not decide whether the fleet SHOULD run. `touch
  STOP` still outranks it: bringup.sh refuses to launch into a halted fleet and
  exits 1, and launchd will keep politely re-checking and keep being refused. To
  stop the fleet permanently, unload this agent — otherwise removing STOP is the
  only thing standing between a reboot and four running lanes.

  INSTALL — this is a human action, deliberately. §10 forbids writing outside the
  workspace, and ~/Library/LaunchAgents is outside it, so this file is tracked here
  and installed by you:

    cp spikes/harness/net.kingfisher.fleet.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/net.kingfisher.fleet.plist
    launchctl start net.kingfisher.fleet          # or just wait 5 minutes

  VERIFY:
    launchctl list | grep kingfisher              # pid or last exit status
    tail -20 /Users/victorianikolenko/kingfisher/bringup.launchd.log

  UNINSTALL:
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/net.kingfisher.fleet.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/net.kingfisher.fleet.plist

  The absolute paths below are pinned on purpose. loop_gate.sh pins ROOT for the
  same reason: CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR was unset and a $(pwd) fallback resolved to the
  wrong directory, leaving the hook inert for a whole session. launchd starts with
  an even emptier environment than a hook does, so nothing here may be relative.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>net.kingfisher.fleet</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>/Users/victorianikolenko/kingfisher/spikes/harness/bringup.sh</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/victorianikolenko/kingfisher</string>

  <!-- Run at login, then re-check every 5 minutes. Idempotent, so a healthy
       fleet makes this a no-op and a dead lane makes it a repair. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>300</integer>

  <!-- Explicitly NOT KeepAlive: bringup.sh exiting 0 is success, not a crash. -->
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <false/>

  <!-- claude is a Homebrew node binary; launchd's PATH does not include
       /opt/homebrew/bin, and run_loop.sh exits 1 with "claude CLI not found"
       without it. That failure is silent from the operator's side, which is why
       the log below is not optional. -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/victorianikolenko/kingfisher/bringup.launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/victorianikolenko/kingfisher/bringup.launchd.log</string>

  <!-- Nice: four lanes plus another project's containers already put this machine
       at loadavg 18 against quiet.sh's limit of 3.5. Bring-up should never be the
       thing that pushes a measurement out of validity. -->
  <key>Nice</key>
  <integer>5</integer>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
